\"Position(x: 4.0, y: 70.0)\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Ordering Systems","anchor":"Ordering-Systems","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order they’re written, except where an ordering constraint requires"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise. A system that must run after one written later, by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", or before one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written earlier, by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", is moved to satisfy the constraint, and every other system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps its written place:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let frame = Schedule {","    Scoring().after(Movement.self)","    Movement()","    Gravity().before(Movement.self)","}","print(frame.names)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\", \"Scoring\"]\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A constraint naming a type with no system in the schedule is ignored, and one naming a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s own type doesn’t order the system against itself. Constraints that form a cycle,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so that no order satisfies them all, trap; build the schedule with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to throw"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Running Systems at the Same Time","anchor":"Running-Systems-at-the-Same-Time","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two systems "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"conflict"}]},{"type":"text","text":" when one writes a type the other reads or writes, or when either has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs conflicting systems in order and the rest at the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time. The world ends as though the systems had run one after another in order, except that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the commands systems queue apply when their wave finishes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, the order they run in rests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only on how they happen to be written. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" lists those pairs, so a test can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keep a schedule free of them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/CyclicOrdering":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An error indicating that the ordering constraints of a schedule’s systems form a cycle, so no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order satisfies them all."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/cyclicordering","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"CyclicOrdering"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"ide